  <h2 class="section-heading">Objectives</h2>
  <p>This course is designed for computer engineering undergraduate students. Its aim is to introduce the terminology, available methods, and ideas in discrete mathematics to future computer scientists/engineers.</p>

  <h2 class="section-heading">Grading Policy</h2>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li><strong>Midterm (40%)</strong> — Counting Principles</li>
    <li><strong>Final (60%)</strong> — Advanced Counting</li>
    <li><strong>Bonus: Participation (?%)</strong> — High-quality contribution during the lectures (questions, answers, etc.) will get instant bonus points, added to exam grades later.</li>
  </ul>

